 <li itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ListItem">
 <a itemprop="url" href="/c/ohgmor90/818-soul-tree"
 rel="nofollow" >
 <span itemprop="name">
 Soul Tree
 </span>
 </a>
 <div itemprop="description">
 <p><strong>Note: The nodes on the soul tree can be purchased in any order</strong></p>
<p>Amount of Soul Points required to fully max out:</p>
<p><strong>Entire Tree</strong> - 15300 Soul Points</p>
<p><strong>Path of Destruction</strong> - 6375 Soul Points<br><strong>Path of Empowerment</strong> - 4200 Soul Points<br><strong>Path of Sundry</strong> - 4725 Soul Points</p>
<hr>
<h3>Path of Destruction (Leftmost Branch)</h3>
<p><strong>Denature:</strong> DoT Damage increases by 2% per rank<br>Costs:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 25<br>II - 50<br>III - 75<br>IV - 100<br>V - 125</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Critical Point:</strong> Increase base crit damage by +5% per rank<br>Costs:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 50<br>II - 100<br>III - 150<br>IV - 200<br>V - 250</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Strike First, No Mercy:</strong> First attack adds +5% damage per rank, expires after 2 turns<br>Costs:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 100<br>II - 200<br>III - 300<br>IV - 400<br>V - 500</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Comeback:</strong> Gain +1 energy per turn when at or below 25% hp<br>Cost:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 1000</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Energy - Back Guarantee:</strong> Killing an enemy grants 1 energy<br>Cost:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 750</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Lil Bit of Crit:</strong> Increase base crit chance by 1% per rank<br>Costs:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 50<br>II - 100<br>III - 150<br>IV - 200<br>V - 250</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Combat Focus:</strong> After meditating, increase your damage by 2% per rank. Lasts 2 turns. (One turn effectively)<br>Costs:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 50<br>II - 100<br>III - 150<br>IV - 200<br>V - 250</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Run That Back:</strong> Failing a minigame or having your attack dodged reduces the skill&#39;s cooldown by 1 turn<br>Costs:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 500</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p>‌</p>
<h3>Path of Empowerment (Middle Branch)</h3>
<p><strong>Enduring Vessel:</strong> Increase base HP by +2 per rank<br>Costs:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 20<br>II - 40<br>III - 60<br>IV - 80<br>V - 100</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Calm Mind:</strong> Reduce Meditate damage vulnerability by -5% per rank<br>Costs:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 50<br>II - 100<br>III - 150</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Battle Renewal:</strong> Increase post-combat healing by +2.5% per rank<br>Costs:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 20<br>II - 40<br>III - 60<br>IV - 80</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Mending:</strong> Heal +0.5 HP at start of turn per rank (this regen does not scale with outgoing and doesn’t appear to be able to be decreased or increased at all)<br>Costs:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 20<br>II - 40<br>III - 60<br>IV - 80<br>V - 100</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Swiftfoot:</strong> Allows to dodge attack while guarding (if dodgeable)<br>Cost</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 1000</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Impervious:</strong> Start the fight with 1 resist<br>Costs:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 750</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Chug Chug Chug:</strong> Grants you an additional potion slot in each category with each update.<br>Costs:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 100<br>II - 200<br>III - 300</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Light Work, No Reaction:</strong> Makes minigame easier by 0.05 per rank<br>Costs:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 50<br>II - 100<br>III - 150<br>IV - 200<br>V - 250</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p>‌</p>
<h3>Path of Sundry (Rightmost Path)</h3>
<p><strong>Essence Eater:</strong> Increase Essence gain by +10% per rank<br>Costs:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 25<br>II - 50<br>III - 75<br>IV - 100<br>V - 125</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Even Further Beyond:</strong> Increase Essence cap by +1 per rank<br>Costs:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 25<br>II - 50<br>III - 75<br>IV - 100<br>V - 125</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Overprepared Adventurer:</strong> Grants starting gear, stacking with each rank<br>Costs + Gears:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 25 + Small Healing Potion x3, Matorr’s Encyclopedia<br>II - 100 + Pickaxe<br>III - 200 + Minor Energy Elixir x5<br>IV - 300 + Explorer Blueprint Unlocked<br>V - 400 + Daze, Self Cure (you need to equip the move in the skills menu)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Friends in High Places:</strong> Illustris portal starts open (this is the portal to Church of Raphion<br>Cost:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 100</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Shifting Origins:</strong> Choose respawn location from attuned spots<br>Cost:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 100</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Path Maker:</strong> Fast Travel spots carry over on death<br>Cost:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 250</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Uninteresting Loan:</strong> Increase starting Gold by +200 per rank<br>Costs:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 25<br>II - 50<br>III - 75<br>IV - 100<br>V - 125</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Escape Artist:</strong> Increase escape chance by +2% per rank (base escape chance is 20% without speed)<br>Costs:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 25<br>II - 50<br>III - 75<br>IV - 100<br>V - 125</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Expert Harvester:</strong> 25% chance for double harvest (stacks with Gatherer from <a href="https://trello.com/c/umfjhJub/187-way-of-life" title="smartCard-inline">https://trello.com/c/umfjhJub/187-way-of-life</a>)<br>Cost:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 500</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Raphion’s Resume:</strong> Reduce Covenant/Class level requirement by -1 per rank (this means you require 1 less level than you would normally to learn/join. Applies to Super, Base and Sub classes)<br>Cost:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 50<br>II - 100<br>III - 150<br>IV - 200<br>V - 250</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Soul Vault:</strong> Unlocks the Soul Vault at the bank, allowing you to carry 1 item through a wipe<br>Cost:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I - 500</p>
</blockquote>
 </div>
 <h4>Labels</h4>
 <ul>
 <li itemprop="keywords">Important</li>
 </ul>
 </li>
 <li itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ListItem">
 <a itemprop="url" href="/c/4NPg9XDC/944-triumphs-%E2%86%91"
 rel="nofollow" >
 <span itemprop="name">
 Triumphs ↑
 </span>
 </a>
 <div itemprop="description">
 <p>Triumphs are objectives that you must complete in order to earn Soul Points. They are divided into two categories: <strong>Repeatable Triumphs</strong> and <strong>First-Time Triumphs</strong>. Enabling <strong>Trials</strong> will multiply the amount of Soul Points you receive.</p>
<p>Repeatable Triumphs can be completed an infinite number of times, while First-Time Triumphs can only be completed once.</p>
<p><strong>Note:</strong> You receive Soul Points only after you wipe and respawn as a new character. Wiping through the Lineage Shard does not grant Soul Points.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Repeatable Triumphs</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Base Class | 15 Soul Points<br>Super Class | 30 Soul Points<br>Max Rank Covenant | 30 Soul Points<br>Obtained an unique enchant | 30 Soul Points<br>Obtained and equipped a unique Artifact | 45 Soul Points</p>
<blockquote>
<p>First time Triumphs</p>
</blockquote>
<p>First Base Class | 20 Soul Points<br>First Super Class | 50 Soul Points<em><br>First Mid Rank covenant | 50 Soul Points<br>First Boss Completed | 50 Soul Points<br>First Artifact Equipped | 75 Soul Points</em><br>First Max Rank covenant | 75 Soul Points*<br>First Mark | 500 Soul Points</p>
 </div>
 <h4>Labels</h4>
 <ul>
 <li itemprop="keywords">Important</li>
 </ul>
 </li>
 <li itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ListItem">
 <a itemprop="url" href="/c/VekmL2BA/1043-move-scaling"
 rel="nofollow" >
 <span itemprop="name">
 Move Scaling
 </span>
 </a>
 <div itemprop="description">
 <p>Practically every damage dealing active in Arcane Lineage scales off of your stats to deal damage. However different moves have varying scalings to determine how much your stats will influence the damage of your attack. The Formula for move scaling is as follows</p>
<blockquote>
<p>BaseDMG(1+(stat/scaling)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>‌</p>
<ul>
<li>BaseDMG means the base damage of your attack</li>
<li>Stat means the stat of the caster of the move if the attack scales with that stat</li>
<li>Scaling is the variable number which every move has which determines how much your stat will determine the damage of your move<ul>
<li>e.g if a move has STR/75 scaling, this means that the scaling is 75 and your strength stat substitutes into STR</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p>For example, if a player has 200 STR and is using Strike, a move with a BaseDMG of 5 and typically has a scaling of STR/75 it would be displayed like this</p>
<blockquote>
<p>5(1+(200/75)</p>
</blockquote>
<p><img src="https://trello.com/1/cards/69cc54d687e5063460908d5d/attachments/69cc57ac09795beb7b1bcf32/previews/69cc57ad09795beb7b1bcf51/download/image.webp" alt="image.webp"></p>
<p>This formula can also be placed into a Desmos Scientific Calculator, which can be found <a href="https://www.desmos.com/scientific" title="‌" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer ugc nofollow">here</a></p>
<p>If you have any DMG multipliers and you are trying to calculate your damage make sure to multiply them at the end</p>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Dual/Multi Scaling</strong></p>
<p>If a move scales with more than one stat the formula of this scaling changes a bit but remains generally the same</p>
<blockquote>
<p>BaseDMG(1+(stat1/scaling1 + stat2/scaling2)</p>
</blockquote>
<ul>
<li>this pattern continues if there is a move which scales on more than 2 stats</li>
</ul>
<p>For example if you have 100 STR and 100 ARC and you use Lifeless Skull, which has a BaseDMG of 13 and scales off of STR and ARC by /80 for both stats, your damage would be calculated by doing the following</p>
<p><img src="https://trello.com/1/cards/69cc54d687e5063460908d5d/attachments/69cc58a52129695f51ffca29/previews/69cc58a52129695f51ffca58/download/image.webp" alt="image.webp"></p>
 </div>
 <h4>Labels</h4>
 <ul>
 <li itemprop="keywords">Important</li>
 </ul>
 </li>
 <li itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ListItem">
 <a itemprop="url" href="/c/rWS0vTkK/1534-invested-stats"
 rel="nofollow" >
 <span itemprop="name">
 Invested Stats
 </span>
 </a>
 <div itemprop="description">
 <h3>Strength</h3>
<p>Does nothing, <em>technically</em></p>
<ul>
<li>Raises your Physical Damage by 1.32% per point</li>
<li><em>However,</em> every move has a scaling number, your Physical Damage % does not go towards this formula<ul>
<li>The Physical Damage % is only an accurate representation of moves which are under /75 scaling</li>
<li>For more information about move scaling, refer to <a href="https://trello.com/c/VekmL2BA/1043-move-scaling" title="smartCard-inline">https://trello.com/c/VekmL2BA/1043-move-scaling</a></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>15% of all of your Strength stat is granted as a bonus buff<ul>
<li>e.g If you have 100 STR, you will get 15 STR as a bonus</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p>‌</p>
<h3>Arcane</h3>
<p>Also does nothing, <em>technically</em></p>
<ul>
<li>Raises your Ranged Damage by 1.32% per point</li>
<li><em>However,</em> every move has a scaling number, your Ranged Damage % does not go towards this formula<ul>
<li>The Ranged Damage % is only an accurate representation of moves which are under /75 scaling</li>
<li>For more information about move scaling, refer to <a href="https://trello.com/c/VekmL2BA/1043-move-scaling" title="smartCard-inline">https://trello.com/c/VekmL2BA/1043-move-scaling</a></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>15% of all of your Arcane stat is granted as a bonus buff<ul>
<li>e.g If you have 100 ARC, you will get 15 ARC as a bonus</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p>‌</p>
<h3>Endurance</h3>
<p>Raises your Endurance stat by 1.3 per stat invested</p>
<p>‌</p>
<h3>Speed</h3>
<p>Lowers your DIFF, increases movement speed and uhhh</p>
<p>‌</p>
<h3>Luck</h3>
<p>Raises your Crit%, your CritDMG, Essence gain, EncounterRegen and Drop Rates</p>
<ul>
<li>Raises your Crit% by 0.5% per stat</li>
<li><del>Raises your CritDMG by ~0.065 per stat</del></li>
<li>Increases your essence gain by ? per stat</li>
</ul>
<p>‌</p>
<ul>
<li>Increases Encounter Regen by 0.5% per stat, stacking additively with itself and other sources of EncounterRegen<ul>
<li>EncounterRegen is the healing received at the end of a fight</li>
<li>At base EncounterRegen heals 19.5% of your MaxHP<ul>
<li>Since you have at least 1 LCK at base, this means the number is typically 20% of your MaxHP</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p>‌</p>
<ul>
<li>Raises the chances for certain items to drop within combat<ul>
<li>This primarily affects the following</li>
<li>Mob alchemy items (Slime Chunk, Sand Core, etc)</li>
<li>Scrolls (excluding lost scrolls?)</li>
<li>Blueprints</li>
<li>Weapon Shards</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Weapon Shards are guaranteed to be a certain tier if you exceed the following LCK amounts<ul>
<li>50 LCK for guaranteed Weak shards from enemies</li>
<li>120 LCK for guaranteed Strong shards from enemies</li>
<li>200 LCK for guaranteed Pure shards from enemies<ul>
<li>Bosses may guarantee certain shard tiers by default, ignoring this system</li>
</ul>
</li>
