 <li itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ListItem">
 <a itemprop="url" href="/c/7KcoHTXv/171-status-effects"
 rel="nofollow" >
 <span itemprop="name">
 Status Effects
 </span>
 </a>
 <div itemprop="description">
 <hr>
<ul>
<li>Poison: Afflicted unit takes damage equal to how many stacks of poison are applied at the start of their turn. This DoT is lethal and can kill the unit.</li>
<li>Bleed: Afflicted unit takes 3% of their max HP as DoT when they act. When the afflicted unit blocks or dodges a hit, it also takes 3% of max HP as damage.</li>
<li>Burn: Afflicted unit takes 0.35% of max HP as DoT at the start of their turn, increasing by 0.1% for every additional stack above 1, capping at 2.25% at 20 stacks.</li>
<li>Ghostflame: Afflicted unit takes 3.85% of Max HP as DoT at the start of their turn.</li>
</ul>
<p>Check <a href="https://trello.com/c/yViy295v/6-dot-info" title="smartCard-inline">https://trello.com/c/yViy295v/6-dot-info</a> for additional Information.</p>
<hr>
<ul>
<li>Vulnerable: Afflicted unit intakes 20% more damage.</li>
<li>Hexed: Afflicted unit&#39;s incoming attack(s) deal double damage and remove one stack per hit. Persists until all stacks are gone.</li>
<li>Blinded: Afflicted unit has an increased QTE difficulty for dodging and class minigames.</li>
<li>Weakened: Afflicted unit deals 20% less damage</li>
<li>Cursed: Afflicted unit decreases Incoming and Outgoing healing by 20% per stack. (it&#39;s bugged right now to where any stack sets outgoing healing at 0)</li>
<li>Stun: Afflicted unit is unable to dodge or block and the next turn is skipped. Taking hits while under this effect removes ONE stack of it.</li>
<li>Heavy Stun: Afflicted unit is unable to dodge or block and the next turn is skipped.</li>
<li>Crippled: Afflicted unit is unable to block and dodge, disable Guarding / Escape for players.</li>
<li>Cold: Using a skill while afflicted makes the cooldown 50% longer than it would be normally</li>
<li>Sundered: Afflicted unit&#39;s Incoming attacks ignore resistances</li>
<li>Fractured: Afflicted unit intakes 35%+ Physical/Magic damage.</li>
<li>Taunted: Afflicted unit will target the player who applied it.</li>
<li>Pressure: Grants a 10X% chance to not gain NRG at the start of the afflicted’s turn. X is the amount of stacks on the afflicted, this cannot be more than 50%</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<ul>
<li>Resist: Afflicted unit has immunity to any status effect until given one, Persists until all stacks are gone. (can&#39;t resist Heavy Stun)</li>
<li>Invisibility: Immune to damage and targeting while also increasing your escape chance, except Metrom’s Vessel’s Oblivion. Status effects still deal damage. Enemies skip their turn if your whole party is invisible. Makes your next attack have 20% dmg increase.</li>
<li>Overheat: Increases damage by 8% and speed by 7.5% per stack. Capped at 10 stacks.</li>
<li>Energized: gives you a 10X% chance to gain additional Energy, X being equal to stacks of Energized</li>
<li>Thorns: Reflect damage? (need test)</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://trello.com/c/xaUHrIuf/102-yarthul-the-blazing-dragon" title="‌">Inferno</a>: Inferno: Lose health per turn based on the amount of stacks applied while also decreasing outgoing and incoming by ? per stack applied. Stacks are consumed via [Blaze Core], [Magma Beam], &amp; [Armageddon]</li>
<li><a href="https://trello.com/c/YWN8kLvt/103-thorian-the-rotten" title="‌">Plague</a>: Each stack of plague decreases the afflicted users damage and defense by an amount that increases per stack applied.</li>
<li><a href="https://trello.com/c/5IOpna8F/248-seraphon" title="‌">Purified</a>: Any form of healing will be directed towards seraphon if the target healing has purified and that player will not be healed (lifesteal aside from parasitic leech does not apply to this and nor does passive regeneration)</li>
</ul>
<p>Credits to <span class="atMention" title="aurill40">@aurill40</span> for the initial list.<br>Credits to <span class="atMention" title="sorenkaz">@sorenkaz</span> for the updated list.<br>Credits to <span class="atMention" title="sachizumi">@sachizumi</span> for revisions.<br>Credits to <span class="atMention" title="k_dagod1">@k_dagod1</span> for being evil.</p>
 </div>
