 <li itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ListItem">
 <a itemprop="url" href="/c/8xlsIKyA/348-mastery"
 rel="nofollow" >
 <span itemprop="name">
 Mastery
 </span>
 </a>
 <div itemprop="description">
 <p><strong>Super Class Mastery Guide</strong><br>-</p>
<p>Mastery Tree its Upgrade Tree for your Super Class, choice <strong>&quot;I&#39;d like to learn more about myself.&quot;</strong> in Trainer dialogue to see it</p>
<hr>
<p>To get Mastery points, you have to kill Bosses and Mobs, Bosses gives more progress to get a mastery point.<br>For Breakthrough Points, you have to consume an <a href="https://trello.com/c/1XnrnrpA/80-echo-shard" title="smartCard-inline">https://trello.com/c/1XnrnrpA/80-echo-shard</a></p>
<p>Mastery points get harder to get the more you already have (kind of works like leveling up)</p>
<hr>
<p>You can only have a max of <strong>35 Mastery Points</strong> and for breakthroughs is how many echo shards you can use. (Only advisable to have 3-4 breakthroughs)</p>
<p>Everytime you wipe, you save your last amount of mastery points, and <em>you can only save <strong>3</strong> of your original breakthroughs</em></p>
<hr>
<p>Mastery have <strong>3</strong> path || <strong>Left / Middle / Right</strong></p>
<p>Every path have <strong>1 Passive</strong> and <strong>1 Skill Proficiency</strong> that required <strong>Breakthrough</strong> points</p>
<p>0-0-0 its Start (no Breakthrough points)<br>1-1-1 its Passives (first Breakthrough points)<br>2-2-2 its Profs (second Breakthrough points)</p>
<p>For example 2-0-0 mean that you get <strong>Passive</strong> and <strong>Proficiency</strong> in left path</p>
<p>Mastery paths such as 2-2-0 and 0-2-2 are exclusions to this, as the 1-0-0 and 0-0-1 nodes are skipped respectively to have enough mastery to get the rest</p>
<hr>
<p>Mastery Tree using Mastery points and Breakthrough points for nodes</p>
 </div>
