 <li itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ListItem">
 <a itemprop="url" href="/c/yViy295v/6-dot-info"
 rel="nofollow" >
 <span itemprop="name">
 DoT Info
 </span>
 </a>
 <div itemprop="description">
 <blockquote>
<p>Bleed:</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Deals a flat 3% of your Max HP whenever the afflicted unit takes the following actions: Using a move, Guarding, Meditating, Escaping. When the afflicted unit blocks or dodges an hit, take 3% of their MaxHP as damage. This DoT does not get affected by modifiers.</p>
<p>‌</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Poison:</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Deals damage to unit equal to total stacks inflicted before turn start. This does not scale with any form of DoT modifiers. This DoT is lethal and can kill the unit.</p>
<p>‌</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Burn:</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Deals 0.7% of the unit&#39;s Max HP on turn start. This damage increases by 0.2% per Burning stack on the opponent. Caps at 20 stacks</p>
<ul>
<li>DoT damage is based on the stacks on the opponent before their turn begins</li>
<li>This DoT&#39;s damage does not scale with statuses inflicted.</li>
</ul>
<p>‌</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Ghostflame:</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Deals 3.85% of max HP at base each turn. Increases by 0.35% for each unique status effect on the target.</p>
<ul>
<li>the DoT damage is calculated before statuses decay</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<p><strong>EXTRA INFO</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Summons do not inherit from your DoT modifiers.</li>
<li>If multiple entities with different DoT modifiers values apply the same effect, the value that effect holds will be from the first source that applied the effect. It stays that way until the effect is removed.</li>
<li>Formulas that increase DoT damage also scale with your DoT multipliers. If a person with no DoT multipliers applies Ghostflame, it will deal 3.85%. If that same person then applies Blinded, the Ghostflame damage will increase by 0.35%. If a person with a maxed Soul Tree applies Blinded, the increase will be higher, even if the Ghostflame was originally applied by someone with no DoT multipliers.</li>
<li>Dark Sigil and Spore Root have a NULL DoT value, meaning that Weaken and Vulnerable effects applied by Dark Sigil, as well as Weaken and Poison applied by Spore Root, will not increase the damage of any DoTs that scale with the number of unique statuses (only Ghostflame for now). Chaos Orb and Enchants have the same DoT value as you do!</li>
<li>MV shares the same DoT resist as other bosses, wings don’t change his DoT resistance.</li>
<li>Poison resistance and fire resistance does not change the damage of burning/poison damage respectively.</li>
</ul>
 </div>
 <h4>Labels</h4>
 <ul>
 <li itemprop="keywords">Additional Info</li>
 </ul>
 </li>
 <li itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ListItem">
 <a itemprop="url" href="/c/tEurzPCV/772-outgoing-and-incoming-healing"
 rel="nofollow" >
 <span itemprop="name">
 Outgoing and Incoming Healing
 </span>
 </a>
 <div itemprop="description">
 <p>Every players starts with 100% outgoing and 100% incoming, this amount can be increased by through various methods, however all forms of in combat healing buffs are ADDITIVE and affect both incoming and outgoing healing.<br>| This means that if a player has 150% outgoing healing, a 50% healing buff will increase this to 200% and not 225%</p>
<p>‌</p>
<p>A players passive regeneration will scale on your outgoing healing, certain methods such as way of life will simply double the end result of your regeneration. Note that a buff that heals you by an amount over a duration of turns will NOT scale with outgoing nor incoming and is a flat unchanged amount.</p>
<p>Lifesteal is not affected by either incoming nor outgoing healing, with the exclusion of <a href="https://trello.com/c/kFO3WPV8/309-parasitic-leech" title="smartCard-inline">https://trello.com/c/kFO3WPV8/309-parasitic-leech</a> since it is considered a heal. When using a healing move on a player, it will cast on the casters outgoing healing alongside with the receiving players incoming healing, plus any additional scalings that the move has (arcane/strength stats for saint moves for example).</p>
<p>‌</p>
<p>For more info on how passive regen works refer to <a href="https://trello.com/c/WAX3l4rC/11-inner-machinations-of-regeneration" title="smartCard-inline">https://trello.com/c/WAX3l4rC/11-inner-machinations-of-regeneration</a></p>
 </div>
 <h4>Labels</h4>
 <ul>
 <li itemprop="keywords">Additional Info</li>
 </ul>
 </li>
 <li itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ListItem">
 <a itemprop="url" href="/c/gZIEskQt/439-diminishing-returns-fatigues"
 rel="nofollow" >
 <span itemprop="name">
 Diminishing returns/Fatigues
 </span>
 </a>
 <div itemprop="description">
 <p>Diminishing returns - Makes the next weapon shard of same type less effective, starts after 2 shards of same type.</p>
<p>100%&gt;100%&gt;25%&gt;25%&gt;25%&gt;25%&gt;25%</p>
<hr>
<p>Block/Dodge fatigue - after each successful dodge or block the bar decreases.</p>
<p>Both blocking and dodging has penalties that reduces block/dodge QTE size equally by 10% for every penalty.</p>
<p>The lowest size the block/dodge QTE can be is 40% of its original size.</p>
<hr>
<p><del>Crit fatigue - Every time you land a crit, your crit chance decreases, if you fail to land crit, your crit chance will reset.</del></p>
 </div>
