 <li itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ListItem">
 <a itemprop="url" href="/c/g9kllebj/1546-heresy"
 rel="nofollow" >
 <span itemprop="name">
 Heresy
 </span>
 </a>
 <div itemprop="description">
 <p>Heresy has two stances, <strong>Dark Wing</strong> and <strong>White Wing</strong>. You always start in <strong>Dark Wing</strong>.</p>
<p>You build up two separate resources, <strong>Dark Force</strong> and <strong>Light Force</strong>. Neither carries over if you leave the form.</p>
<p>Gaining <strong>Corrupt Power</strong> also grants <strong>Force 1:1</strong> into whichever stance you&#39;re currently in.</p>
<p>Attacking grants <strong>Force</strong> to whichever resource your current stance builds (<strong>Dark Force</strong> in <strong>Dark Wing</strong>, <strong>Light Force</strong> in <strong>White Wing</strong>): a flat amount per hit, plus a bonus on landing a crit (once per turn, scaling with crit tier).</p>
<p>(<strong>Light Force</strong> is also gained from <strong>Daybreak</strong> deflecting a status off of you.)</p>
<p>‌</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Dark Wing</strong>: Inflicting <strong>Bleeding</strong>, <strong>Burning</strong>, or <strong>Poisoned</strong> on an enemy also creates a <strong>Shadow</strong> copy of that status on yourself, used later by <strong>White Wing&#39;s</strong> Conversions. Failing to apply a status grants <strong>Corrupt Power</strong>. As a bonus action that doesn&#39;t cost your turn, you can spend 25/50/75/100% of your <strong>Light Force</strong> pool to gain <strong>Crit Rate</strong> 1:1 on your next attack, expiring after 3 turns if unused.</li>
</ul>
<p>‌</p>
<ul>
<li><p><strong>White Wing</strong>: <strong>Daybreak</strong> rerolls any status about to be inflicted on you, with the odds scaling off your <strong>Light Force</strong>. Successfully applying a status grants <strong>Corrupt Power</strong>. As a bonus action that doesn&#39;t cost your turn, you can spend <strong>50 Dark Force</strong> to trigger a <strong>Conversion</strong>, detonating one of your <strong>Shadow</strong> statuses for an effect based on which status it was.</p>
<pre><code> **Conversions**: Spend 50 **Dark Force** to detonate a **Shadow** status. One per turn, bonus action (does not cost your turn). All three now require selecting a target.</code></pre>
</li>
</ul>
<p>‌</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Burning</strong> -&gt; <strong>Detonate</strong> + <strong>Shadowflamed</strong>: Instantly procs all <strong>Burning</strong> and <strong>Ghostflamed</strong> on the target (Burning 0.5% + 0.2% of max HP per stack, capped at 20 stacks; <strong>Ghostflamed</strong> flat 3.5% of max HP). Then applies <strong>Shadowflamed</strong> for 3 turns: +30% damage to both <strong>Burning</strong> and <strong>Ghostflamed</strong> on that target.</li>
</ul>
<p>‌</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Bleeding</strong> -&gt; Creates a healing pool worth 0.5% of the <strong>TARGET&#39;s</strong> max health per stack, capped at 5%. Split across your party weighted by how much health each ally is missing. Skips <strong>Incoming/Outgoing</strong> since this is a bonus action.</li>
</ul>
<p>‌</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Poisoned</strong> -&gt; <strong>Contagion</strong>: Reshapes the <strong>Poison</strong> already on the target instead of adding damage. Alone against one enemy, poison stacks x1.10. Against several, the target&#39;s stacks x0.90 and every other living enemy is seeded with 20% of the original stack count as fresh <strong>Poison</strong>. </li>
</ul>
<p>‌</p>
<p><strong>Recoil</strong> is generated from gaining <strong>Corrupt Power</strong> and from holding <strong>Shadow</strong> statuses, and <strong>White Wing</strong> also generates it from each <strong>Daybreak</strong> deflection. <strong>Recoil</strong> is reduced by removing a <strong>Shadow</strong> status from yourself, landing crits, or applying statuses.</p>
<p>‌</p>
<p>When your form ends, your <strong>Recoil</strong> will trigger a backlash mechanic, dealing <strong>Max Health</strong> damage to you based off of the amount of <strong>Recoil</strong> you had when losing your form. This is triggered no matter how the form ends.</p>
<p>‌</p>
<h2>Heresy Variants</h2>
