<p>‌</p>
<p>Can also drop any <a href="https://trello.com/c/Z5eW4t0g/465-%E2%A0%80" title="smartCard-inline">https://trello.com/c/Z5eW4t0g/465-%E2%A0%80</a> of any tier, any scroll including <a href="https://trello.com/c/BaCK7KSW/117-lost-scrolls" title="smartCard-inline">https://trello.com/c/BaCK7KSW/117-lost-scrolls</a> and blueprints.</p>
<hr>
<h3><em>HP/Affinities</em></h3>
<p>HP: 10000, he will have 15000 if he is corrupted</p>
<ul>
<li>Takes 90% Hex/Dark type damage</li>
<li>Takes 110% Nature type damage</li>
<li>Takes 120% Holy type damage</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h1><strong>PASSIVES</strong></h1>
<p><strong>General Passives</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Has an unknown chance to gain 2 energy instead of one per turn</li>
<li>Regenerates 50(?) hp per turn</li>
<li>Immune to the Stun and Cursed status effect</li>
<li>Metrom’s Amulet will heal this boss instead of dealing damage</li>
<li>Cannot have statuses from <a href="https://trello.com/c/1MY4Wlji/62-darkblood-weapons" title="smartCard-inline">https://trello.com/c/1MY4Wlji/62-darkblood-weapons</a> reflected upon him</li>
<li>Has two turns where most enemies would typically have one (statuses will decay and DoT will take effect on both of these turns)</li>
<li>Cannot be killed before he enters his second phase, if he is brought down to 100 hp before his second phase, he will heal back to 5k hp</li>
<li>This enemy can block and dodge attacks</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Phase 1</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Spawns with 6 wings, these heavily decrease the damage he takes per wing active, whenever an instance of a status effect is applied or he uses eclipse a wing will disappear, when all wings disappear he enters an offensive state, altering some of his moves and letting him use his ultimate ability, oblivion</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Phase 2</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Metrom’s Vessel starts in an offensive state where he deals more damage than usual. After taking ~500 damage he will enter his defense state, where he takes and deals notably less damage. He will swap back to his offensive state after ? turns</li>
<li>If Metrom’s Vessel was at 100 hp before he entered his second phase, he will permanently stay in his offensive state (most likely a bug)</li>
<li>Metrom’s Vessel will always use his offensive variations of moves that he would use in his first phase, regardless of his state within this phase</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<h1><strong>MOVES</strong></h1>
<h3><strong>Priority Moves</strong></h3>
<h6><em>The boss will almost always attempt to use these moves first if the conditions are met, the moves are ordered in what holds the highest priority</em></h6>
<p><strong>Unyielding Fury</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><em>2 Energy | CD 11 | <strong>DARK type</strong></em></li>
<li>Condition: Metrom’s is in his second phase</li>
<li>Status move</li>
<li>| Applies 2 hex and 3 blinded to all opponents and negates their energy gain for 2 turns while also locking out their ability to meditate</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Oblivion</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><em>5 Energy | CD 11 | <strong>DARK type</strong></em></li>
<li>Condition: Metrom’s is in his offensive state and has 5 energy</li>
<li>Multihit (20) | AOE | Unblockable/Undodgeable</li>
<li>| Hits everyone on the opposition for exactly 50% of their total hp as damage, applies 1 cursed, 2 weakened and 2 blinded whilst corrupted and decreases outgoing and incoming healing by 50% for the next 2 turns. This move becomes altered while corrupted</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Invoke Shadeblades</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><em>3 Energy | <strong>DARK type</strong></em></li>
<li>Condition: Metrom’s Vessel has 3 energy and at he is missing at least 1 summon</li>
<li>Status move</li>
<li>| Summons 2 <a href="https://trello.com/c/Egd6CyDV/774-shadeblade" title="smartCard-inline">https://trello.com/c/Egd6CyDV/774-shadeblade</a> , if there is already 1 Shadeblade on the field, this will only summon 1 Shadeblade. Metrom’s Vessel can only have 2 Shadeblades active at once</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Deathbound</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><em>2 Energy | CD 7 | <strong>DARK type</strong></em></li>
<li>Condition: Metrom’s Vessel has 2 energy</li>
<li>Single hit | Semi AOE | Undodgeable</li>
<li>| 15 Base Damage, hits two targets and will apply 2 sundered towards them. Loses its priority when Metrom’s Vessel is in Phase 2</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Eclipse</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><em>0 Energy | CD 4 | <strong>HEX(?) type</strong></em></li>
<li>Condition: All above priority moves are on cooldown</li>
<li>Status move</li>
<li>| Effect: Increases Metrom’s Vessel damage notably, if he is in his second phase and in a defensive state, all physical damage dealt towards him shall be reflected 1:1 with whoever dealt the damage for the next two turns. Loses priority when Metrom’s Vessel is in Phase 2</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Mini Shadebringer</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><em>0 Energy | CD 4 | <strong>DARK type</strong></em></li>
<li>Condition: Metrom’s Vessel is in his second phase</li>
<li>Multihit (3) | Single Target | Unblockable/Undodgable</li>
<li>| 4 Base Damage, the damage of this attack will increase the longer Metrom’s Vessel is within his offensive state in Phase 2</li>
</ul>
<h3><strong>Non-Priority Moves</strong></h3>
<h6><em>The general moves Metrom’s Vessel will use if the conditions of other moves are not met, moves are ordered in terms of their energy cost, not anything else</em></h6>
<p><strong>Rending Slash</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><em>0 Energy | CD 0 | <strong>PHYSICAL type</strong></em></li>
<li>Single hit | Single Target | Blockable/Dodgeable</li>
<li>| 13 Base Damage, ignores half of defense on block/guard and applies 3 weakened on hit</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Shadebringer</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><em>1 Energy | CD 5 | <strong>DARK type</strong></em></li>
<li>Multihit (3) | AOE | Unblockable/Undodgeable</li>
<li>| 8 Base Damage, if Metrom’s Vessel is within his defensive state in Phase 1, this will be single target and will apply 1 cursed per hit if the attack is not blocked, this attack can never be dodged naturally.</li>
<li>If Metrom’s Vessel is in his offensive state or Phase 2, this attack will become fully AOE, becoming unblockable and undodgeable always and applying 1 cursed per hit (The attack appears to be blockable but is currently bugged and isn’t supposed to act this way, it can be blocked if you’re solo because of this as well)</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Blackout</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><em>2 Energy | CD 4 | <strong>DARK type</strong></em></li>
<li>Single hit | Single Target/AOE | Dodgeable</li>
<li>| 10 base damage, while Metrom’s Vessel is in his defense mode in Phase 1, this move is a single target attack that can be dodged, if the move hits, your last used move will have its cooldown extended.</li>
<li>If Metrom’s Vessel is in his offensive state or Phase 2, this attack becomes fully AOE, becoming unblockable and undodgeable always and extending the cooldowns of everyone’s last used move. This move might deal less damage while in this mode than usual</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Hexed Rend</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><em>3 Energy | CD 6 | <strong>HEX type</strong></em></li>
<li>Single hit | Single Target/AOE | Dodgeable</li>
<li>| 16 base damage, while Metrom’s Vessel is in his defense mode in Phase 1, this move is a single target attack that can be dodged (and for most non-speed builds also blocked). If the move hits, it applies 1 hexed and 1 cursed onto the target</li>
<li>If Metrom’s Vessel is in his offensive state or Phase 2, this attack becomes fully AOE, becoming unblockable and undodgeable always, however it loses its capability to apply statuses.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Corrupted Variations</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Deathbound:</strong> Now applies 3 sundered instead of 2</li>
<li><strong>Invoke Shadeblades:</strong> Shadeblades will have 300 hp when summoned instead of 200 hp</li>
<li><strong>Oblivion:</strong> Now applies 2 cursed, 5 weakened, 5 blinded and deals 60% of a player’s total hp instead of 50%</li>
</ul>
 </div>
