 <div itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ItemList">
 <h3 itemprop="name">Tests &amp; Speculations</h3>
 <ol>
 <li itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ListItem">
 <a itemprop="url" href="/c/XdIDxGlK/100-narthanas-average-healing-proc"
 rel="nofollow" >
 <span itemprop="name">
 Narthanas Average healing proc
 </span>
 </a>
 <div itemprop="description">
 <h1>Topic: Testing Narthana&#39;s Sigil Proc Threshold</h1>
<p>Personnel in charge: honk<br>test subject name: jimbo the slime</p>
<h2><strong>Procedure</strong></h2>
<ul>
<li>Rejoin between tests to refresh any invisible effects (namely possible overheal carryover)</li>
<li>start an encounter (lava encounter were used for these tests, not that that&#39;s important)</li>
<li>spawn slime &gt; let slime get as low as possible to prevent overheal.</li>
<li>start with holy grace then swap between lesser heal and cleansing prayer for smaller/more accurate intervals</li>
</ul>
<h2><strong>- Tests:</strong></h2>
<p>--Test 1--<br>1 120.3 grace<br>2 29.3 lesser<br>3 98.5 grace &lt;- narthana&#39;s procs<br>total: 248.1</p>
<p>--Test 2--<br>1 39.8 lesser<br>2 38.5 cleansing<br>3 100.5 holy grace<br>4 21.8 lesser<br>5 28.3 cleansing<br>6 17.8 lesser<br>7 17.2 cleansing<br>8 136.4 holy grace &lt;- narthana&#39;s procs (grace was overkill here, ideally keep doing lesser/cleansing for smaller heals)<br>total 400.3</p>
<p>--Test 3--<br>test 3<br>1 136.4 holy grace<br>2 38.5 cleansing<br>3 42.8 lesser<br>4 38.5 cleansing<br>5 39.8 lesser &lt;- narthana&#39;s procs<br>total 296</p>
<p>--Test 4--<br>1 100.5 holy grace<br>2 28.3 cleansing<br>3 29.3 lesser<br>4 38.5 cleansing<br>5 29.3 lesser<br>6 38.5 cleansing<br>7 39.8 lesser &lt;- narthana&#39;s procs<br>total 304.2</p>
<p>--Test 5--<br>1 60.9 grace<br>2 17.2 cleansing<br>3 21.8 lesser<br>4 136.4 grace<br>5 17.2 cleansing<br>6 17.8 lesser &lt;- narthana&#39;s procs<br>total 271.3</p>
<ul>
<li>Results:</li>
</ul>
<hr>
<p>Average proc requirement: <strong>303.98 healing</strong><br>This i only a speculation knowing there MIGHT be a third party for proccing narthanas</p>
 </div>
 </li>
 <li itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ListItem">
 <a itemprop="url" href="/c/V2s63X8E/115-dragon-icerind-blight-weapon-thoroughly-passive-dmg-test"
 rel="nofollow" >
 <span itemprop="name">
 Dragon / Icerind / Blight weapon thoroughly passive &amp; dmg Test
 </span>
 </a>
 <div itemprop="description">
 <h1>Topic: Testing weapon damage buff and cursed applying from blight weapon</h1>
<p>Personnel in charge: Claw, Honk<br>Damage test subject name: Honk<br>Cursed test subject name: Claw, Honk</p>
<h2><strong>Procedures for damage test</strong></h2>
<p>Get slime encounter<br>Test damage without debuffs<br>Test damage with debuffs</p>
<h2><strong>Procedures for cursed applying test</strong></h2>
<p>Get encounter<br>Hit enemies without debuffs<br>Hit enemies with debuffs</p>
<h1>Damage test</h1>
<p>-# No weapon<br>Fists to vulnerable 8.2<br>Fists to nothing 6.8</p>
<p>-# blight dagger<br>Blight dagger to weakened and vulnerable 9.8<br>Blight dagger to vulnerable 9.8<br>Blight dagger to weakened 8.2<br>Blight dagger to nothing 6.8</p>
<p>-# blight staff<br>Blight staff to weakened crit 14.3<br>Blight staff to vulnerable 9.8<br>Blight staff to weakened 8.2<br>Blight staff to nothing 6.8</p>
<p>-# dragon weapon (tested only sword)<br>Dragon sword to burn 7.8<br>Dragon sword to nothing 6.8</p>
<p>-# icerind weapon (tested only on greatsword)<br>Icerind greatsword to cold 9.8<br>Icerind greatsword to nothing 8.2</p>
<h1>Cursed applying test</h1>
<p><strong>Dagger</strong><br>-# without debuffs<br>11 hits no cursed</p>
<p>-# with debuffs<br>First hit cursed (weakened, blind, cold)<br>Second hit cursed (weakened, blind, cold)<br>Third hit cursed (weakened, blind, cold)<br>Fourth hit cursed (weakened, blind, cold)<br>Fifth hit cursed (vulnerable)</p>
<p><strong>Staff</strong><br>-# without debuffs<br>10 hits no cursed</p>
<p>-# with debuffs<br>First hit cursed (weakened, blind, cold)<br>Second hit cursed (weakened, blind, cold)<br>Third hit cursed (weakened, blind, cold)<br>Fourth hit cursed (weakened, blind, cold)<br>Fifth hit cursed (vulnerable, blind)</p>
<h1>extra test</h1>
<p><strong>Dagger</strong><br>-# tested with bleed/poison<br>First hit no cursed (bleed)<br>Second hit no cursed (poison)</p>
<h2><strong>Results</strong></h2>
<p>Dragon weapon 15% buff<br>Blight weapon 20% buff<br>Icerind Weapon 20% buff</p>
<p>Blight weapon apply cursed only if enemy have weakened or vulnerable (guaranteed)</p>
 </div>
 </li>
 <li itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ListItem">
 <a itemprop="url" href="/c/L1LZFz8w/185-paladin-test-1"
 rel="nofollow" >
 <span itemprop="name">
 Paladin test #1
 </span>
 </a>
 <div itemprop="description">
 <h1>Topic: Shield Testing</h1>
<p>Personnel in charge: honk<br>punching bag: FastSmash_37 (no soul tree, paladin)</p>
<h2><strong>Procedures for dmg reduction</strong></h2>
<ul>
<li>begin an encounter (with one or more slimes)</li>
<li>let the slime use smack on you. dont block, dont guard.</li>
<li>let the slime use smack on you. block</li>
<li>let the slime use smack on you. guard</li>
<li>repeat for every shield<br>-write down the numbers, ezpz.</li>
</ul>
<h2><strong>Procedures for dmg reflection</strong></h2>
<p>this only applies to the dragonflame shield.</p>
<ul>
<li>begin an encounter (with one or more slimes)</li>
<li>let the slime use smack on you. block</li>
<li>let the slime use smack on you. guard</li>
<li>test concluded.</li>
</ul>
<h2><strong>Results</strong></h2>
<ul>
<li>see image for results, im not typing it all out.<br>--Notes--</li>
<li>the dragonflame shield&#39;s dmg reflection is reduced by guarding. (what affects this requires it&#39;s own testing. i suspect defense buffs do not affect the dmg reflected)</li>
<li>the slimy buckler&#39;s weaken debuff applies to the melee hit that proc&#39;d it, effectively increasing it&#39;s dmg reduction. this puts it on par with the towershield for dmg reduction against melee attacks, but slightly worse than the towershield against ranged attacks. (this also means lentum&#39;s slimy shield passive&#39;s weaken also works the same way.)</li>
</ul>
 </div>
 </li>
 <li itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ListItem">
 <a itemprop="url" href="/c/BjVkWcAh/184-paladin-test-2"
 rel="nofollow" >
 <span itemprop="name">
 Paladin test #2
 </span>
 </a>
 <div itemprop="description">
 <h1>Topic: Dragonflame Shield Dmg Reflection %</h1>
<p>Personnel in charge: honk<br>punching bag: QuickCrash63/FastSmash_37</p>
<p>just a fun continuation on this series.</p>
<ul>
<li>This test is to determine what percentage the dmg you take the dragonflame shield reflects.<br>(keep in mind, your defense buffs dont matter, the dmg is almost entirely based on the attacker&#39;s dmg.)</li>
</ul>
<h2><strong>Procedures</strong></h2>
<ul>
<li>begin with ur completely clean alt account. (no class, soul tree, artifacts, accessories, etc etc)</li>
<li>get into an encounter (with one or more slimes)</li>
<li>let the slime use smack. dont block/guard</li>
<li>let the slime use smack. block</li>
<li>let the slime use smack. guard</li>
<li>write down the dmg u take, and ur done with this step. these are your control values.</li>
<li>swap to your completely clean alternative alt account (has nothing as stated earlier, only have the paladin super class for the shield passive)</li>
<li>let the slime use smack. dont block/guard</li>
<li>let the slime use smack. block</li>
<li>let the slime use smack. guard</li>
<li>write down the values for the dmg you took and the dmg you reflected for each.<br>-all done</li>
</ul>
<h2><strong>Results</strong></h2>
<p>fuck this shield</p>
<ul>
<li>anyways it reflects a staggering 2x the dmg of the attack.</li>
<li>guarding are the only things that reduce its dmg.</li>
<li>the reflected dmg bypasses innate resistances (check thief testing values. thieves have a 10% physical dmg resistance)</li>
<li>also this shows that guarding and blocking dont increase your defense, they more specifically directly lower the dmg of the attack you block/guard against. (not that that matters tho)</li>
</ul>
 </div>
 </li>
 <li itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/ListItem">
 <a itemprop="url" href="/c/0S9WsUj3/183-paladin-test-3"
 rel="nofollow" >
 <span itemprop="name">
 Paladin test #3
 </span>
 </a>
 <div itemprop="description">
 <h1>Topic: Paladin&#39;s Shield Training Passive</h1>
<p>Personnel in charge: honk<br>punching bag: QuickCrash63/FastSmash36</p>
<ul>
<li>this test is to determine the significance of the passive&#39;s affects; namely dmg reduction for allies &amp; dmg the paladin takes</li>
</ul>
<h2><strong>Procedures</strong></h2>
<ul>
<li>begin with ur completely clean alt account. (no class, soul tree, artifacts, accessories, etc etc)</li>
<li>party up with ur paladin slot.</li>
<li>get into an encounter (with one or more thieves)</li>
<li>let the thief use strike. dont block/guard with either account.</li>
<li>write down the dmg u take, and ur done with this step. these are your control values.</li>
<li>begin with ur completely clean alt account. (no class, soul tree, artifacts, accessories, etc etc)</li>
<li>party up with ur paladin slot.</li>
<li>get into an encounter (with one or more thieves)</li>
<li>let the thief use strike. dont guard/block with the clean account. guard with the paladin account.</li>
<li>record the values as per usual. (if ur paladin is using a dragonflame shield, then also note the dmg reflected. otherwise, repeat the previous 5 steps with the shield afterwards.)</li>
</ul>
<h2><strong>Results</strong></h2>
<ul>
<li>the paladin&#39;s shield effects (dragonflame&#39;s dmg reflection, slimy buckler&#39;s debuffs, icerind shield&#39;s debuffs) carry over to the hit the ally takes.</li>
<li>the dmg the dragonflame shield reflects is based on the dmg the paladin actually takes, not the total dmg absorbed/the dmg the ally takes.</li>
<li>allies only take ~50% of the original attack&#39;s dmg.</li>
<li>neither the dmg the ally takes nor the dmg the paladin takes is affected by the shield they use.</li>
</ul>
 </div>
